WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:06.665
Ethan was thinking hard as he walked to the playground.

2
00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:12.890
It was almost the end of summer camp, and he was sad.

3
00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:16.293
He didn't know if he'd see Mr.

4
00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:17.855
Dunn after camp was over.

5
00:00:19.236 --> 00:00:20.317
He wanted to give Mr.

6
00:00:20.357 --> 00:00:23.280
Dunn something that would show how much everyone liked camp.

7
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.462
He wanted it to be something that would help Mr.

8
00:00:26.502 --> 00:00:27.944
Dunn to remember everyone.

9
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:33.000
"Hey, Ethan," Mr.

10
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:33.561
Dunn said cheerfully.

11
00:00:33.581 --> 00:00:34.482
"Did you bring your empty soda bottle?"

12
00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:36.603
Ethan pulled a bottle out of his backpack.

13
00:00:36.623 --> 00:00:37.404
"What is it for?"

14
00:00:37.424 --> 00:00:41.387
"We're going to use it to make a terrarium."

15
00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:44.750
Mr. Dunn held up a package of seeds.

16
00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.473
"Has anyone ever heard of a terrarium?"

17
00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:49.414
he asked.

18
00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:54.178
"Ooh, my pet frog, Gurpy, lives in a terrarium!

19
00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.942
Wow! Are we growing frogs, Mr.

20
00:00:59.982 --> 00:01:01.844
Dunn? Are we?"

21
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.761
Izzie asked excitedly.

22
00:01:04.802 --> 00:01:05.863
Mr. Dunn laughed.

23
00:01:06.523 --> 00:01:09.425
"Terrariums can be for animals or plants.

24
00:01:10.586 --> 00:01:13.148
We're going to plant seeds in our bottles.

25
00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:15.329
Not frogs.

26
00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.171
Sorry, Izzie."

27
00:01:18.351 --> 00:01:19.172
Ethan giggled.

28
00:01:20.793 --> 00:01:22.374
Poor Izzie looked disappointed.

29
00:01:22.394 --> 00:01:27.077
"But first we need to get some pebbles and soil."

30
00:01:28.118 --> 00:01:30.340
Mr. Dunn held up large paper cups.

31
00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:37.603
"Let's head to the Mr.

32
00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:40.124
Dunn pointed to the ground underneath a tree.

33
00:01:40.144 --> 00:01:42.765
"Here's a good place to get soil."

34
00:01:46.146 --> 00:01:48.147
Ethan stuck a cup into the soil.

35
00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:52.569
"Is it okay if we scoop up worms?"

36
00:01:52.589 --> 00:01:57.992
"A soda bottle is a pretty small home for a worm," Mr.

37
00:01:58.032 --> 00:01:58.632
Dunn said.

38
00:01:59.764 --> 00:02:02.065
"Let's leave the worms out here in the woods."

39
00:02:03.386 --> 00:02:04.186
Ethan nodded.

40
00:02:04.206 --> 00:02:06.908
Mr. Dunn always had good answers.

41
00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.771
The kids were ready to create their terrariums.

42
00:02:11.791 --> 00:02:16.733
"First we have to cut our bottles," said Mr.

43
00:02:16.773 --> 00:02:20.976
Dunn. "We're going to use the bottom part for planting."

44
00:02:22.016 --> 00:02:24.798
He told the campers to draw a line on the bottle.

45
00:02:24.818 --> 00:02:29.060
"Make it about 12 centimeters from the bottom."

46
00:02:30.452 --> 00:02:32.954
"Mr. Dunn likes to garden," Ethan thought.

47
00:02:34.115 --> 00:02:35.736
Maybe the campers could get Mr.

48
00:02:35.796 --> 00:02:36.496
Dunn a shovel.

49
00:02:37.417 --> 00:02:38.958
How much did shovels cost?

50
00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.441
Mr. Dunn helped everyone cut their bottles.

51
00:02:45.803 --> 00:02:47.885
Then they were ready for pebbles and soil.

52
00:02:47.905 --> 00:02:54.629
"Place one layer of pebbles on the bottom of your terrarium.

53
00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.952
Then fill the terrarium with soil.

54
00:02:59.016 --> 00:03:03.217
Leave about four centimeters of room at the top," said Mr.

55
00:03:03.277 --> 00:03:05.938
Dunn. "Then add seeds.

56
00:03:07.278 --> 00:03:10.059
You can grow grass, clover, or basil."

57
00:03:11.519 --> 00:03:12.580
Ethan followed Mr.

58
00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.720
Dunn's instructions.

59
00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:20.042
He sprinkled a handful of clover seeds in his terrarium and covered them with soil.

60
00:03:24.923 --> 00:03:27.664
lightly water your seeds with a spray bottle.

61
00:03:28.748 --> 00:03:30.168
Don't soak the soil.

62
00:03:31.229 --> 00:03:33.529
It only needs to be moist," Mr.

63
00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:34.210
Dunn said.

64
00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:38.171
"I actually lost my watering can at home.

65
00:03:39.331 --> 00:03:42.732
So I've been watering my indoor plants with this spray bottle!"

66
00:03:43.012 --> 00:03:43.992
Mr. Dunn said.

67
00:03:44.012 --> 00:03:46.553
"That's it!"

68
00:03:46.913 --> 00:03:47.693
Ethan thought.

69
00:03:48.893 --> 00:03:52.514
A watering can would be the perfect gift from the Kids Central kids!

70
00:03:54.155 --> 00:03:57.956
The campers fitted the top halves of their bottles back on their terrariums.

71
00:03:59.141 --> 00:04:01.125
Ethan thought about his idea for Mr.

72
00:04:01.145 --> 00:04:01.846
Dunn's gift.

73
00:04:02.988 --> 00:04:05.133
The last day of camp was going to be sad.

74
00:04:06.215 --> 00:04:07.377
But when they gave Mr.

75
00:04:07.417 --> 00:04:10.343
Dunn the watering can, everyone would be happy!
